<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mwene Mutapa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mwene <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> was the title of the king of the Mutapa Empire, a term from which the state itself took its name. The ruler stood at the apex of a hierarchy of nobles, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spirit-medium">spirit mediums</a> and commoners. His authority combined political and religious roles and was reinforced by displays of military power that kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> chiefs loyal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mwene-mutapa.jpg" alt="Mwene Mutapa" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SweetCanadianMullet · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:ZimbabweStatesAndTrade.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
